WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:09.580
Over the past 35 years, North Korea has developed
both nuclear weapons and missiles to deliver

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.580
them.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:11.580
How did this happen?

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:15.379
The North Korea nuclear crisis dates back
to 1980, when a spy satellite detected nuclear

00:00:15.379 --> 00:00:18.410
reactor construction north of Pyongyang.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:23.160
In 1992, Secretary of State James Baker won
a Denuclearization Declaration in which both

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.710
Koreas foreswore the work to build a bomb.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.000
Still, Pyongyang’s plutonium stocks surged.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.820
Bill Clinton sought to keep North Korea in
the Non-Proliferation Treaty.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.500
This culminated in the 1994 Agreed Framework.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.920
Pyongyang agreed to abandon its bomb program
for reactors and fuel.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.019
North Korea later admitted it began cheating
almost immediately.

00:00:41.019 --> 00:00:44.219
Once again, America sought to assuage North
Korea with incentives.

00:00:44.219 --> 00:00:47.219
Secretary of State Condoleezza Rice even lifted
sanctions.

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:48.760
Once again, the North cheated.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.399
In 2006, it tested a nuclear bomb.

00:00:51.399 --> 00:00:54.370
As for Obama, he ignored North Korea to focus
on Iran.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.930
The problem is North Korea views diplomacy
less as a means to peace and more as a way

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.299
to buy time.

00:00:59.299 --> 00:01:02.729
Diplomacy is not a religion to be worshipped
blindly nor a cost-free option.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:16.500
Indeed, when it comes to Korea, its price
may one day be counted in millions 

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:23.850
of lives.

